// coop_net.cpp -- module 1: session, config, file IO, the wire codec, the
// cmd.txt harness, sync.txt, the heartbeat, the main loop scheduler
// (OnTick -> 30/15/2/1 Hz) and the shared base layer every other module leans
// on (log, coop_dir.txt, the real-time clock, ue:: object helpers).
//
// Ported from mod/CoopMod/Scripts/main.lua, READ-ONLY reference:
//   24-153    config/DIR/ME/ROLE, actorTail, now, log, writeFile, readLine,
//             safe, fullname, validActor, isLive
//   154-187   getWorld/getPC/getPawn/locOf/dist/runConsole/playerChars
//   1409-1451 peerFile, parseKV, section
//   1566-1606 sendOwn                       (net::Publish)
//   1936-1983 applyPeer                     (net::ApplyPeer)
//   2055-2196 lookTestTick, runCommands     (net::RunCommands + LookTestTick)
//   3957-3988 streamStatus part, writeSyncStatus (net::WriteSyncStatus)
//   3989-4133 guards, step, heartbeat, onGame/runLoop, the three loops, boot
//             emit, stale-file cleanup, "=== CoopMod start ==="
//
// The wire format is byte-compatible with relay/cooprelay.py: one JSON line per
// file, field order and number formats frozen (docs/NATIVE-PORT.md section 2.3).
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// CONTRACT-REQUESTs (things this module needs that coop_state.h / ms2_ue.h as
// shipped do not provide; all are worked around here, none blocks a build)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 1. ms2_ue.h has no ue::GetWorld / GetPlayerController / GetPawn /
//    ConsoleCommand / MakeFName / GetCDO even though the porting brief lists
//    them.  net resolves world/PC/pawn itself (GameplayStatics::
//    GetPlayerController over every live UWorld, cached) and runs
//    ExecuteConsoleCommand through ue::Call.  When the engine layer grows the
//    fast path, net::World/PC/Pawn/Console should switch to it -- the caching
//    and the guard behaviour stay.
// 2. combat::NearestNpc(&key, &actor) / combat::CollectNpcs(): cmd.txt's
//    kill / hurt / hp / aitest / npctp need the *sorted* collectNPCs() list
//    (main.lua:1265-1317).  net keeps a deliberately reduced private copy
//    (nearest first, same 4000 uu radius, same enemy/turret preference) because
//    the real ordering needs combat's PEER_CLAIMS / ownership bias.
// 3. appear::QueueLookAdd(const std::string& path): cmd.txt `lookadd` needs to
//    hand a path to appear's LOOK_ADD/LOOK_TEST (main.lua:2061-2078).  net uses
//    appear::SetLookAdded() for the result and diffs FindAllOf(<class>) itself.
// 4. puppet::RequestGameLoad(const std::string& path): net::Find(path, true)
//    cannot queue a load (LOAD_ON.txt).  Default is off in Lua too, so this only
//    matters with LOAD_ON.txt present; net logs once and keeps going.
// 5. RESOLVED: puppet::StartTp / puppet::StartTravel are declared in
//    coop_state.h section 10 and this file calls them; PuppetState is written only
//    by its owner (the header's "owner writes" rule holds).
// 6. RESOLVED: MontageSig has no `at`, and needs none -- PeerState::at IS the
//    packet clock, and ApplyPeer sets it on exactly the fresh-packet condition
//    that sets the montage (main.lua:1963-1972).  coop_puppet reads
//    state().peer.at for the montage play head.
// 7. RESOLVED: CombatState::spawnAlias is a string -> string map (StrStrMap), one
//    table shared by coop_combat (writer) and coop_local (reader).
// 8. LocalState::wpns is documented as "the section body" while the Lua's
//    MYWPNS carries the enclosing brackets.  net::Publish normalises both.
// 9. RESOLVED: `bool coop::net::ReadText(const std::string&, std::string*)`
//    (whole-file read, coop_world's ledger) is declared in coop_state.h and
//    defined here.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

